                                    <h1>Eid al-Adha Marketing Playbook for D2C Brands 2026-2027</h1>
                                    <p>Eid al-Adha (Bakri Eid + Feast of Sacrifice) is the second major Islamic festival after Eid al-Fitr — 10th of Dhu al-Hijjah + Hajj completion + sacrifice + family + community celebration. UAE + Saudi + Indonesia + Malaysia + India Muslim + global Muslim diaspora. Distinct occasion from Ramadan Eid al-Fitr — sacrifice + family + gathering focus. Here is the complete playbook.</p>
                                    <h2>Eid al-Adha vs Eid al-Fitr Difference</h2>
                                    <p><strong>Eid al-Fitr (Ramadan Eid):</strong> Post-Ramadan celebration + charity + community + gifting + peak Muslim retail.<br><strong>Eid al-Adha (Bakri Eid):</strong> Post-Hajj + sacrifice commemoration + family + gathering + specific occasion.<br>Both major but different themes:<br>- Eid al-Fitr peak retail + gifting + broad celebration.<br>- Eid al-Adha family + gathering + sacrifice + F&amp;B focus + more focused occasion.<br><strong>Retail size:</strong> Eid al-Fitr larger retail season. Eid al-Adha smaller but still significant.</p>
                                    <h2>Eid al-Adha Timeline</h2>
                                    <p><strong>4-6 weeks before Eid:</strong> Planning + inventory + campaign design begins.<br><strong>2-4 weeks before (Dhu al-Hijjah start):</strong> Pre-Eid campaigns launch + Hajj-adjacent content.<br><strong>Week of Hajj (peak Hajj days):</strong> Peak Hajj-adjacent campaigns.<br><strong>Eid al-Adha day (10th Dhu al-Hijjah):</strong> Peak occasion celebration.<br><strong>3-day Eid celebration:</strong> Continued celebration + F&amp;B + family gathering.<br><strong>Post-Eid week:</strong> Post-Eid gratitude + community + wellness reset.</p>
                                    <h2>Eid al-Adha Category Coverage</h2>
                                    <p><strong>F&amp;B + halal meat:</strong> Peak category — halal meat + F&amp;B for sacrifice + celebration.<br><strong>Traditional attire + occasion wear:</strong> Traditional Muslim attire + occasion clothing.<br><strong>Home + gathering essentials:</strong> Home + hosting + gathering + gift essentials.<br><strong>Perfume + oud + fragrance:</strong> Traditional + luxury fragrance gifting.<br><strong>Wellness + beauty gifting:</strong> Beauty + wellness + gift essentials.<br><strong>Kids + gifts:</strong> Kids gifts + Eidi + celebration items.<br><strong>Home + décor:</strong> Islamic home + décor + gift items.<br><strong>Hajj-adjacent:</strong> Hajj travel + gift + adjacent products.</p>
                                    <h2>Regional Playbook Priorities</h2>
                                    <p><strong>UAE:</strong> Eid al-Adha significant + retail + family + gift focused. 15-25% of Ramadan Eid scale.<br><strong>Saudi:</strong> Peak Eid al-Adha market — Hajj + sacrifice + family. Similar to Ramadan Eid scale.<br><strong>Indonesia + Malaysia:</strong> Muslim-majority + significant Eid al-Adha celebration.<br><strong>India (Muslim + Bakri Eid):</strong> Bakri Eid + traditional celebration + halal + F&amp;B focus.<br><strong>Bangladesh + Pakistan:</strong> Significant Eid al-Adha + family + celebration.<br><strong>Diaspora (USA + UK + Australia):</strong> Diaspora Muslim community Eid al-Adha celebration.</p>
                                    <h2>Content + Creative Playbook</h2>
                                    <p>Eid al-Adha content playbook:<br><strong>Family + gathering emphasis:</strong> Family + gathering + community celebration.<br><strong>Sacrifice + tradition storytelling:</strong> Sacrifice + tradition + heritage storytelling.<br><strong>Hajj-adjacent content:</strong> Hajj + spiritual + Islamic content.<br><strong>F&amp;B + halal celebration:</strong> Traditional + celebration food + halal + community.<br><strong>Traditional + modern balance:</strong> Traditional attire + décor + modern reinterpretation.<br><strong>Regional language content:</strong> Arabic + Urdu + regional languages.<br><strong>Sensitivity + respect:</strong> Cultural + religious sensitivity + respect.</p>
                                    <h2>Regulatory + Cultural Sensitivity</h2>
                                    <p><strong>Halal certification:</strong> Essential for F&amp;B + product credibility.<br><strong>Islamic-appropriate imagery:</strong> Modest + Islamic-appropriate imagery + models.<br><strong>Cultural + regional sensitivity:</strong> Distinct regional Islamic traditions + variations.<br><strong>Charity + Zakat integration:</strong> Charity + Zakat + community give-back.<br><strong>Language + Arabic content:</strong> Arabic + regional-language essential.<br><strong>Prayer time + Islamic calendar sensitivity:</strong> Islamic calendar + prayer time sensitivity.<br><strong>Non-Muslim brand messaging:</strong> Non-Muslim brands must approach with cultural respect + authenticity.</p>

